% A fermata lengthens the note, rest or chord that it decorates, but the
% bar check counts the length written in the bar.  checkbar() (genmidi.c)
% counted the length played, so that each bar with a fermata but the
% first one was reported as too long, an error with -Werror.  The
% fermatas below are on notes, rests, chords, a staccato note, a trill, a
% tuplet and a tied note, in and out of a repeat.  Tune 2 plays them with
% %%MIDI fermatafixed.
X:1
T:Fermatas in the bars
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
C D E F |Hc d e Hz |H[ce] a H[ce]2 |
|: H.c d HTe f |(3Hcde f g :| Hc-c a b |!fermata!c d e f |]

X:2
T:Fermatas in the bars, fermatafixed
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
%%MIDI fermatafixed
C D E F |Hc d e Hz |H[ce] a H[ce]2 |
|: H.c d HTe f |(3Hcde f g :| Hc-c a b |!fermata!c d e f |]
